s  this time he looks even more comic  accurate good luck to the guys who had  to carry him out of the ring  Star Trek appreciation Bryan Singer  isn't ashamed of being a Trekkie  when we visit storms home her television  is playing the original Star Trek series  season 2 episode who mourns for a  geneious this Trek episode foreshadows  future events with apocalypse as it  focuses on the team encountering a  powerful godlike character who can grow  to amazing Heights sound familiar  singer also appeared as an uncredited  crew member in Star Trek nemesis taking  orders from the  professor Eck's himself Patrick Stewart  Stanley's cameo co-star we've seen Stan  Lee cameo as a postman Hugh Hefner Larry  King and intergalactic ladies man and  even a strip club DJ get made up in  x-men apocalypse these role is much  simpler we see him react to something  horrific the big difference from his  previous cameos is who's with him this  time around with Lee during the scene is  his real-life wife Joan reloading weapon  X the last x-men apocalypse trailer  teased Hugh Jackman's returned for the  we've lost counting time as Wolverine  the film gives Logan his adamantium  skeleton from the Weapon X program  rewriting origins story even further  along with his trademark trauma-induced  berserker rage  best of all Jackman actually wears the  iconic Weapon X headgear straight from  the comics don't hold your breath for  the characters famous yellow spandex  costume though another order of the  Phoenix  speaking of Wolverine the characters  longtime love interest Jean Grey is only  in her teens during the film and she's  still struggling to control her powers  Jean Grey has nightmares about what's  going to happen teasing the inevitable  fight against apocalypses forces she  also alludes to seeing flames and a  darkness inside of her  foreshadowing her character's eventual  possession by the cosmic entity known as  the Phoenix in both x-men The Last Stand  and the original comic books